# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TickTrack UK - environment configuration
#
# EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS OPTIONAL. The app runs with no .env file at all:
# the Elanco API needs no key, and OpenStreetMap tiles need no account.
# Copy this file only if you want to override a default.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser by Vite.
# Never put a private secret in a VITE_ variable - it would be readable by
# every visitor in the shipped bundle.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -- Elanco Tick Sightings API ----------------------------------------------
# Public, read-only, no API key required, CORS open for browser calls.
# The app falls back to this exact value if unset. Override it to point at a
# mock server or a local proxy while developing offline.
# VITE_ELANCO_API_BASE_URL=https://dev-task.elancoapps.com/data

# -- Map tiles --------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to the OpenStreetMap standard raster layer. Override to use another
# XYZ raster provider. If you change the URL you MUST also change the
# attribution to match that provider's terms - it is a licence requirement,
# not a formality.
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL=https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# VITE_MAP_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors

# -- Maximum upload size for sighting photographs, in megabytes -------------
# Defaults to 5. Images are downscaled to 1280px on the long edge before being
# stored, so this caps the file a user may choose, not what is kept.
# Client-side validation only - see the README's "Known limitations".
# VITE_MAX_IMAGE_SIZE_MB=5
